/ Stage 4 (ruling 8) — the two guards don't move. `set %n% = 5` has no `as`, so the step
/ names no Type (the number is read from the literal form); `set %s% = "hi" as text` is a
/ force, and text stays text. Both green today — stage 4 must keep them green.
NoAsNoType
- set %n% = 5
- assert.equals(Expected="number", Actual=%n!type.name%, Message="bare literal: form gives number")
- set %s% = "hi" as text
- assert.equals(Expected="text", Actual=%s!type.name%, Message="as text stays text")
